  from the frozen mutators, because a /tmp binary's correspondence to its diff is exactly the thing no cheap check
  establishes, and this project has twice paid for a binary that outlived the source it was believed to match.

  TWO LEGS ARE NOT MUTANTS OF THE FIX AND ARE THE TABLE'S IDENTITY ROWS (floor clause (c)):
      noff  -- dev_8253.c's own flip-flop toggle neutered (`^= 1' -> `^= 0').  It touches NO lca code.  It is the
               NEGATIVE CONTROL FOR THE NEW CHANNEL: if the pit rows are vacuous, noff is green.
      nox   -- dev_pckbc.c's stub counter with its `x++' removed: the liveness control for the stub alternator.

================================================================================================================
PRE-TABLE CHECK 1 -- SIBLING PARITY
================================================================================================================
  pit0 / pit1 / pit2 are siblings (counters 0/1/2 = lanes 0/1/2) and are PARITY-MATCHED at 37 rows each:
  3 liveness + 16 store + 16 load + 2 cross-direction.  No asymmetry, so no row is owed.
  ASYMMETRY FOUND AND DISPOSED OF, TWICE:
    (a) LANE 3 HAS NO pit SESSION.  Port 0x43 is the mode register: a read returns `mode_byte' with no side effect
        and advances NO flip-flop, so the alternator does not exist there.  This is MEASURED, not reasoned --
        `cdxZL3', whose entire edit is at lane 3, scores 150/150 against the prototype pit rows
        (opus_c5_20260915/logs2/laneC1.out).  Lane 3 therefore keeps `stub3' + its mandatory liveness row, and
        repair 6 adds `stub3 z1' for the lane-3 x zero-data joint.  DISCLOSED with its measurement.
    (b) pit0's sibling behaviour DIFFERS INSIDE THE DEVICE: an MSB write to counter 0 calls `timer_add' /
        `timer_update_frequency' (hz = 1193182/counter) where counters 1 and 2 emit an unlatched `fatal()'.  The
        probe keeps counter 0's programmed value LARGE (~250 Hz) so no high-frequency host timer is installed.
        No row is owed -- the asymmetry is in the ORACLE's neighbourhood, not in a channel any lca mutant reaches.

