PRE-TABLE CHECK 2 -- CLAIM -> ROW  (semantic trigger: does this added sentence assert something a row could see?)
================================================================================================================
  "the flip-flop advance ... fires on EVERY counter access, read and write"        -> every `ps*B' / `pl*B' row.
  "`wr_msb' and `rd_msb' are SEPARATE PER DIRECTION, which is why a read-parity row
   is blind to an added WRITE and the PW shape exists"                             -> `pit* pw r1/r2',
                                                                                      `pitT pw t6/t6B/t3/t3B'.
  "a control word REWINDS both flip-flops, so every phase is self-starting"        -> `pit* live1/live2'.
  "lane 3 is unreachable on this channel"                                          -> EXPLICIT NO-ROW SENTENCE,
                                                                                      carrying its measurement
                                                                                      (cdxZL3 150/150).
  "the unlatched `fatal()' flood moves no row -- the probe parses `print' output"  -> DISCHARGED BY `base' ITSELF:
      if the flood perturbed the instrument, base could not be 352/352.  Filed separately as `pit8253flood'.
  "one command must produce EXACTLY ONE reply"                                     -> `kbcmd <w> pre/pop/post'.

